Recommends: python3-pip
Suggests: tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-fra, pulseaudio-utils | alsa-utils
Description: notes organised by topic, lockable with a password
 Scrinium keeps short notes (numbers, procedures, codes) as cards grouped by
 topic, automatically saved as plain text files.
 .
 Each note can be locked with a password (AES-256-GCM, scrypt-derived key). An
 optional rescue file, created by the user, can reopen a note whose password
 was forgotten. The interface is available in French and English.
